		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Baofeng DM-1801 specific • Re: Hard Reset.]]></title>

					<category term="Baofeng DM-1801 specific" scheme="http://localhost/opengd77/viewforum.php?f=17" label="Baofeng DM-1801 specific"/>
		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5130&amp;p=37146#p37146"><![CDATA[
in the official firmware?<br><br>with the radio off...<br><br>press and hold <strong class="text-strong">SK1 Key</strong> + <strong class="text-strong">Key 1</strong> and turn on the radio, you will see <strong class="text-strong">Memory Reset?</strong> in the screen, and then confirm with Menu button and the led will flash in orange color for few seconds, and then it will be factory reset/hard reset.<br><br>in OpenGD77 firmware?<br><br>with the radio off...<br><br>press and hold the <strong class="text-strong">SK2 key</strong> and turn on the radio, you will see <strong class="text-strong">Settings Updated</strong> in the screen (that will reset settings only), and after that open the OpenGD77 CPS and write a new codeplug (that will reset the other things).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4191">MELERIX</a> — Sun May 18, 2025 12:49 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
